Maya (Docs): Heads-up: I started a lightweight PR to add a "stream recovery" troubleshooting card to errref. Goal: one-page guidance for when streams die mid-response (how to resume vs fallback), plus tiny JS + curl snippets and a migration note about the Retry-After-ms header. PR: https://git.internal/redwood/docs/pull/3488

Raj (SDK): nice. i'll contribute the SDK-normalization snippet and a short test. Quick note: SDK now accepts both Retry-After (seconds) and Retry-After-ms. we normalize to milliseconds like this: 

```js
// normalize Retry-After header (accepts sec or ms)
function parseRetryAfter(hdr) {
  if (!hdr) return 1000;
  const n = parseInt(hdr, 10);
  if (isNaN(n)) return 1000;
  // heuristic: values > 1000 are likely ms
  return n > 1000 ? n : n * 1000;
}
```

Raj (SDK): i'll add this to the snippet and mention the heuristic in a one-line comment.

Zoe (EngRuntime): runtime emits two related codes: `stream_interrupted` (with metadata partial_tokens) and `rate_limited` (with retry_hint). Important: sometimes both happen in the same request path. Recommend doc guidance: prefer serving to an alternate lower-throughput variant instead of retry storms.

Maya (Docs): proposed troubleshooting steps (will include as bullet checklist): 1) look at metrics: is 429 spike bursty or sustained? 2) check retry_hint vs Retry-After-ms value 3) if partial_tokens present, decide resume vs new non-streaming request 4) if concurrent 429s & stream_interrupted, prefer model variant fallback 5) for context_length_exceeded, trim prompt client-side before retry. keeping it very short.

Lina (PM): add one short migration blurb: "We standardized Retry-After values to allow millisecond precision in high-throughput infra paths. Clients should handle both sec and ms formats during migration window (Q2)."

Raj (SDK): agree. also adding an explicit example for resuming from saved KV: 

```js
// resume flow (pseudo)
const resp = await client.streamGenerate({ prompt, stream: true });
if (resp.code === 'stream_interrupted') {
  const partial = resp.metadata?.partial_tokens || 0;
  // either resume if KV persisted
  if (kvSaved) {
    await client.generate({ prompt: resumePromptFromKV() });
  } else {
    // fallback to non-streaming, trim prompt if context error previously
    await sleep(parseRetryAfter(resp.headers['retry-after']));
    await client.generate({ prompt: trimPrompt(prompt) });
  }
}
```

Maya (Docs): i'll keep code blocks short; for curl example i'll show how to read the retry header and handle resume guidance as a note, not a script.

